From: OpenX6X00 <noreply@rf.guru>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: rtw88: coex: no Bluetooth TDMA slot without a Bluetooth link

With a shared antenna (the X6200's RTL8723DU) and Bluetooth idle with no
link at all (COEX_BTSTATUS_NCON_IDLE), rtw_coex_action_bt_idle() still
reserved a TDMA slot for Bluetooth: case 3 while WiFi was idle, 7 or 17
once busy, and "busy" only after a hold-off. Every burst of WiFi uplink
started at a third of its rate: 12 and 9 Mbit/s for the first 10 s, then
25-34 (mean 25.6); with TDMA off and the busy table (12), 33-35 Mbit/s
from the first second (mean 31.8), tried through debugfs and then built.
Page and inquiry scan still win the PTA by their priority, and a
connected or paging Bluetooth keeps its own cases (bt_inquiry, bt_idle
with CON_IDLE, the profile actions).
---
--- a/coex.c
+++ b/coex.c
@@ -1740,16 +1740,18 @@ static void rtw_coex_action_bt_idle(struct rtw_dev *rtwdev)
 
 	if (efuse->share_ant) {
 		/* Shared-Ant */
-		if (!coex_stat->wl_gl_busy) {
+		if (coex_dm->bt_status == COEX_BTSTATUS_NCON_IDLE) {
+			/* No Bluetooth link: a TDMA slot would serve nothing (page
+			 * and inquiry scan win the PTA by their own priority), so
+			 * WiFi keeps the air. With case 3 when idle and 7/17 once
+			 * busy, every burst of an RTL8723DU's uplink began at a
+			 * third of its rate until the busy hold-off ran out.
+			 */
+			table_case = 12;
+			tdma_case = 0;
+		} else if (!coex_stat->wl_gl_busy) {
 			table_case = 10;
 			tdma_case = 3;
-		} else if (coex_dm->bt_status == COEX_BTSTATUS_NCON_IDLE) {
-			table_case = 11;
-
-			if (coex_stat->lo_pri_rx + coex_stat->lo_pri_tx > 250)
-				tdma_case = 17;
-			else
-				tdma_case = 7;
 		} else {
 			table_case = 12;
 			tdma_case = 7;
